  "description": "VICFES crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C39 H91 O14 Yb5. From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb5 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.257-4.627 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 85.88-171.40°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C39H91O14Yb5.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
